  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-7-PPR-250000708</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With Dutch earmarked contribution to the Gender Equality work of the OECD DAC, extra support is provided to the Programme of Work + Budget 2025-2026.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Gender equality team of OECD DAC carries out its part of the  Programme of Work and Budget. With this one-time voluntary contribution, the following activities can be carried out: 

1) Implement DAC Guidance and DAC Recommendation on Gender Equality
2) Provide analysis of development finance on gender equality 
3) Implement the DAC Recommendation on Ending SEAH
4) Develop policy recommendations to integrate gender 
5) Mainstream gender equality in the workstreams of the OECD Development Co-operation Directorate (DCD) and by the OECD. 

The organisation fits the purpose of Social Development Department /Task Force Women&apos;s Rights &amp; Gender Equality to strengthen gendermainstreaming. It meets the policy goal of the minister, focussing on effectiveness of policies by mainstreaming gender, including in priority areas as economic empowerment, health and humanitarian aid.

Gendernet is unique as it can influence the policies of DAC countries on gender and has proven to be reliable partner.</narrative>
  </description>
